<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bahram Chobin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 591</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Bahram VI</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bahram Chobin was a Sasanian general of the Mihran family who defeated the Turks in 588–589. Dismissed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hormizd-iv">Hormizd IV</a> after a setback against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a>, he rebelled and, after Hormizd's overthrow, drove the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a> from the throne, ruling as Bahram VI in 590–591. Khosrow returned with help from the emperor Maurice and defeated him; Bahram fled to the Turks and was murdered. He became a hero of Persian romance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bahram-chobin.jpg" alt="Bahram Chobin" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BahramChobinCoinHistoryofIran.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
